{{RemovedContent}}{{SwitchExclusive}}
'''Serial Codes''' were special codes that could be input in the game for various rewards. This feature was removed in mobile versions alongside the [[Invite Friends to get Moneko]] feature in the [[Version 4.3 Update]] and is defunct in [[Minna de Nyanko Daisensou|Minna De Nyanko Daisensou]] as the game ended its live service. Serial Codes as of now are only applicable in the [[The Battle Cats Unite!|Nintendo Switch version]] as some rewards require this method to be unlocked.

''Note: You must have a linked Nintendo Account in order to claim any bonuses from serial codes in the Nintendo Switch version.''

==Classification and Function==
===Gift Codes===
These were one-time use codes that were sent to the winners of PONOS' contests. These codes would give the player items such as XP, [[Cat Food]] and [[Cat Capsule|Tickets]].

===Secret Codes===
These were codes that when used, would unlock hidden [[Cat Units]].

===Merchandise Codes===
These were one-time use codes that were included alongside Battle Cats merchandise (or in the case of [[Mob Cat (Special Cat)|Mob Cat]] and the 5 [[Kishidan Collaboration Event|Kishidan]] [[Kishidan Collaboration Event|Collaboration]] Units, movie tickets and CDs). They would give items or [[Cat Units]].

